#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# meijer_g_reduce

#% text
# `meijer_g_reduce(e, x)` writes `e` as a combination of Meijer G functions of `x`, kept inactive: `inactive(meijer_g)(a, b, z)` or `inactive(meijer_g)(a, b, z, r)`, which is `G(z^(1/r))`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The representations are those of the Mellin transforms of the functions (for `x > 0`): trigonometric, hyperbolic and exponential functions, logarithms, inverse trigonometric functions, Bessel J and K, Airy functions, `hypergeometric_1f1` and `hypergeometric_2f1`, complete elliptic integrals, `sin_integral`, `exp_integral_ei`, Legendre functions, unit steps and boxes, and powers of binomials `(c + r)^(-s)`.

#% item
# Sums reduce term by term; constant factors and powers of `x` stay outside; some products of two functions have a single representation (two Bessel J functions of one argument, `asin(x)/sqrt(1 - x^2)`, `log(x) unit_step(1 - |x|)`, `acsc(x) unit_step(|x| - 1)`).

#% item
# `activate` turns the result into ordinary Meijer G functions. An expression that has no representation stays unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
meijer_g_reduce(sin(x), x)
#% output
#= pi^(1/2)*inactive(meijer_g)([[], []], [[1/2], [0]], (1/2)*x, 1/2)

#% cell
meijer_g_reduce(bessel_j(1, a*x), x)
#% output
#= inactive(meijer_g)([[], []], [[1/2], [-1/2]], (1/2)*a*x, 1/2)

#% cell
meijer_g_reduce(1/(2*x + 3), x)
#% output
#= (1/3)*inactive(meijer_g)([[0], []], [[0], []], (2/3)*x)

#% cell
meijer_g_reduce(log(x), x)
#% output
#= -inactive(meijer_g)([[1, 1], []], [[1], [0]], x, -1) + inactive(meijer_g)([[1, 1], []], [[1], [0]], x)

#% cell
meijer_g_reduce(hypergeometric_2f1(a, b, c, x), x)
#% output
#= gamma(c)*inactive(meijer_g)([[1 - a, 1 - b], []], [[0], [1 - c]], -x)/(gamma(a)*gamma(b))

#% cell
meijer_g_reduce(bessel_j(2*nu, x)*bessel_j(2*mu, x), x)
#% output
#= inactive(meijer_g)([[0, 1/2], []], [[mu + nu], [-mu - nu, mu - nu, nu - mu]], x, 1/2)/pi^(1/2)

#% text
# The function again:

#% cell
activate(meijer_g_reduce(1/(1 + x^2), x))
#% output
#= (1 + x^2)^-1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `meijer_g`, `fox_h_reduce`, `fox_h`, `inactive`, `activate`
